{"allowed_english": [], "context": {"approved_glossary_entries": [], "generation_contexts": [{"context_id": "sha256:d027975e687aa0ac33c5c8cde0cad18b8dfb7bca48e56feeefa0dea804fe224c", "hash": "sha256:d027975e687aa0ac33c5c8cde0cad18b8dfb7bca48e56feeefa0dea804fe224c", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 464707, "byte_start": 464477, "file": "morphisms.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:ca35e56d34b912746ab5ec25b9d32c6a9a810c48d77897165d4662351b76395b", "line_end": 12606, "line_start": 12602}, "owner_tag": "01RR", "parent_tag": "01RR", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01RR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$g$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:29b2afaec9f4c2ae16bdd9fb00fed63b2efb108faada5dbefaab9bdfaf8ffb39", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:54a56526c4cb1a2661ae78b6d3c5cb06cf86db951868af197108a734af22efb5", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nWe say that two morphisms <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> as in (1) of the definition\ndefine the same rational map instead of saying that they are equivalent.\nIn some cases rational maps are determined by maps on local rings\nat generic points.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0fc9b2f505fb310ced1b09a1f08fee6c6f8d3b8b5f08b4ea073c583f1332cb6d", "unit_id": "inventory:morphisms:01RR:paragraph/0002"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:ff49ff2f2ed30fc04e3741f772461aef595d793273bff86b08c38a5a6f81a46a", "hash": "sha256:ff49ff2f2ed30fc04e3741f772461aef595d793273bff86b08c38a5a6f81a46a", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 466573, "byte_start": 465749, "file": "morphisms.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:bbc6b30e1e7994fb852e892611585f6fe64e1a0b8e0c827c4a69934ff6a339e2", "line_end": 12658, "line_start": 12641}, "owner_tag": "0BX8", "parent_tag": "01RR", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01RR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$x_i$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$Z_1, \\ldots, Z_n$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$X \\setminus \\bigcup_{i \\not = j} Z_i \\cap Z_j$", "MATH_0008": "$X$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "MATH_0010": "$X$", "MATH_0011": "$x$", "MATH_0012": "$s \\in S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-morphism-defined-local-ring}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:29030f705635c9b1b628761d8dbeaad21f9ae79f2fcce7841ec3115bb10146e6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b441fc1b7e75beef991d8f6bee83eb1388c3729e6c1d45720debee24467272f7", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nObserve that any dense open of <MATH_0001> contains the points <MATH_0002>\nso the construction makes sense. To prove (1) or (2)\nwe may replace <MATH_0003> by any dense open. Thus if <MATH_0004>\nare the irreducible components of <MATH_0005>, then we may replace\n<MATH_0006> by <MATH_0007>.\nAfter doing this <MATH_0008> is the disjoint union of its irreducible\ncomponents (viewed as open and closed subschemes). Then both the\nright hand side and the left hand side of the arrow are products\nover the irreducible components and we reduce to the case where\n<MATH_0009> is irreducible.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nAssume <MATH_0010> is irreducible with generic point <MATH_0011> lying over <MATH_0012>.\nPart (1) follows from part (1) of\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nParts (2) and (3) follow from part (2) of the same lemma.\n<STRUCT_0004>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:17ea8ae249abf06f